# Conventions for docs/

## Directory layout

| Directory | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `decisions/` | Architectural decision records (ADRs) in MADR v3 format |
| `design/` | Design documents for subsystem architectures and interface contracts |
| `references/` | Stable reference material for agent context |
| `research/` | Point-in-time research outputs |

## Linting

All Markdown files must pass both rumdl and vale with zero warnings and errors.

**Fixing lint issues:** run `just lint-docs` to check all docs.

**Just recipes:**

| Recipe | What it runs |
|---|---|
| `just lint-docs [files]` | All doc linting (markdown + prose) |
| `just lint-markdown [files]` | `uvx rumdl check` |
| `just lint-prose [files]` | `uvx vale` |

All recipes default to `.` (whole project) when called without file arguments.

**No unilateral suppressions:** never add file-level or global suppressions for rumdl or vale without asking the user first. To add project-specific vocabulary for vale, add entries to `.vale/config/vocabularies/{{ project_slug }}/accept.txt` in alphabetical order.

## Conventions

- Use ATX-style headings, dash list markers, and backtick code fences
